==================================================================
DAY 21 - PART B: LAB (CHECKPOINT PROJECT)
Frontend + backend talking by DNS, exposed through Ingress
Time: 90 minutes
==================================================================

GOAL
----
Namespace "shop" with:
  - backend: your Flask app (YOURUSER/myapp:v1), 2 replicas, Service
    "api" on port 80
  - frontend: nginx that serves a page AND proxies /api to the backend
    by Service DNS name
  - Ingress: host shop.local -> frontend
Then troubleshoot 3 injected faults.

Use the kind-lab cluster with the ingress controller from Day 19.


STEP 1: Backend
---------------
mkdir -p ~/k8s-journey/manifests/week3/shop && cd $_

Write backend.yaml yourself:
  Deployment "api": 2 replicas, image YOURUSER/myapp:v1,
  containerPort 5000, label app=api
  Service "api": port 80 -> targetPort 5000


STEP 2: Frontend config (nginx reverse proxy)
---------------------------------------------
vi frontend-config.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: frontend-nginx
data:
  default.conf: |
    server {
      listen 80;
      location / {
        default_type text/html;
        return 200 '<h1>Shop frontend</h1><p>Try /api</p>\n';
      }
      location /api {
        proxy_pass http://api.shop.svc.cluster.local/;
      }
    }

(ConfigMaps are Week 4; here it just delivers a config file.)


STEP 3: Frontend Deployment and Service
---------------------------------------
vi frontend.yaml

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: frontend
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels: {app: frontend}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: {app: frontend}
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: nginx
        image: nginx:1.27
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
        volumeMounts:
        - name: conf
          mountPath: /etc/nginx/conf.d
      volumes:
      - name: conf
        configMap:
          name: frontend-nginx
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: frontend
spec:
  selector: {app: frontend}
  ports:
  - port: 80
    targetPort: 80


STEP 4: Ingress
---------------
Write ingress.yaml yourself: host shop.local, path / Prefix ->
Service frontend port 80, ingressClassName nginx.


STEP 5: Deploy everything
-------------------------
k create ns shop
k apply -n shop -f .
k get all,ingress -n shop

curl -H "Host: shop.local" localhost/
curl -H "Host: shop.local" localhost/api
curl -H "Host: shop.local" localhost/api       # repeat: different backend pods

Expected: the /api calls show "Hello from v1! Served by container:
api-xxxx" with changing pod names.


STEP 6: Fault injection (ask someone, or do it yourself and forget)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
Apply each fault, observe the symptom, find the cause using ONLY
get/describe/logs/endpointslices/nslookup, then fix.

Fault 1:
  k patch svc api -n shop -p '{"spec":{"ports":[{"port":80,"targetPort":5001}]}}'
Fault 2:
  k patch svc api -n shop -p '{"spec":{"selector":{"app":"apii"}}}'
Fault 3:
  k patch ingress <your-ingress-name> -n shop --type=json \
    -p '[{"op":"replace","path":"/spec/rules/0/host","value":"shopp.local"}]'

For each, write: symptom (status code / error), the command that
revealed the cause, the fix. Restore with: k apply -n shop -f .


STEP 7: Success criteria
------------------------
[ ] / returns the frontend page through the Ingress
[ ] /api returns backend responses from different pods
[ ] Frontend reaches backend only by DNS name (no IPs anywhere)
[ ] All 3 faults diagnosed and fixed
[ ] k delete ns shop && k create ns shop && k apply -n shop -f .
    brings everything back


